<deck title="ahre images" />

# Images in a deck

Drop a real image onto a slide with `<img src="…" />` — drawn with your
terminal's graphics protocol (kitty, iTerm2, Sixel), or Unicode halfblocks as a
fallback.

<img src="sample.png" />

The `src` path is resolved against the deck file's directory.

---

## Sized and centered

Set the display size in cells with `width` / `height` — the image scales to it,
keeping its aspect ratio (give one and the other is derived). It centers on its
own row.

<img src="sample.png" width="24" />

---

## A missing image

When the file can't be loaded, the `alt` text is shown instead — so a broken
path never blanks the slide.

<img src="does-not-exist.png" alt="(diagram unavailable)" />
